{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01MMVD8KtA8dUh3vwbE5u93N", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.mentalfloss.com/technology/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.mentalfloss.com/posts/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for\"}, {\"url\": \"https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for-.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://blogs.arubanetworks.com/?p=8975\"}, {\"url\": \"https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for-.html/amp\"}, {\"url\": \"https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for.html/amp\"}, {\"url\": \"https://ca.news.yahoo.com/people-just-realising-wi-fi-120648036.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://prod-ccroc-direct.merriam-webster.com/wordplay/what-does-wi-fi-really-mean\"}, {\"url\": \"https://lr.eu.psf.lt/r/Jeopardy/comments/1dv5uvm/wifi_means_nothing\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:05:14.860Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Phil Belanger Boing Boing 2005 Wi-Fi doesn't stand for anything WECA", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_018tieMgjWn5t7JYZurHy4p1", "content": [{"title": "what does wi fi stand for", "url": "https://www.mentalfloss.com/technology/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for"}, {"title": "What Does ‘Wi-Fi’ Stand For? It’s Complicated", "url": "https://www.mentalfloss.com/posts/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for"}, {"title": "wifi isnt short for", "url": "https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for.html"}, {"title": "wifi isnt short for", "url": "https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for-.html"}, {"title": "blogs.arubanetworks.com", "url": "https://blogs.arubanetworks.com/?p=8975"}, {"title": "boingboing.net", "url": "https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for-.html/amp"}, {"title": "boingboing.net", "url": "https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for.html/amp"}, {"title": "People Are Just Realising What Wi-Fi Stands For, And We're Shocked", "url": "https://ca.news.yahoo.com/people-just-realising-wi-fi-120648036.html"}, {"title": "What Does 'Wi-Fi' Really Mean?", "url": "https://prod-ccroc-direct.merriam-webster.com/wordplay/what-does-wi-fi-really-mean"}, {"title": "r/Jeopardy Jul 04 '24", "url": "https://lr.eu.psf.lt/r/Jeopardy/comments/1dv5uvm/wifi_means_nothing"}]}, "Phil Belanger, a founding member of the Wi-Fi Alliance (formerly WECA), has said the name has no literal meaning. In his November 2005 post on Boing Boing, he wrote that \"Wi-Fi doesn't stand for anything.\" It is not an acronym. There is no meaning. Several other outlets repeat that quote and attribute it to him.\n\nThe name came from outside the group. Wi-Fi and the ying yang style logo were invented by Interbrand. According to Belanger's account, the founders wanted something catchier than the technical label, and Interbrand also created other brand names like Prozac and Compaq.\n\nThe \"wireless fidelity\" idea traces to a tagline. Belanger said the group briefly used \"The Standard for Wireless Fidelity\" on its materials, and he later called that a mistake that only served to confuse people and dilute the brand. He attributed the tagline to colleagues who didn't understand branding or marketing. Mental Floss notes that the Oxford English Dictionary calls the \"wireless fidelity\" explanation \"spurious.\"\n\nBelanger's claim is from a first-hand source, but it is his account, and the Wi-Fi Alliance's earlier messaging did lean on the tagline."], "durationSeconds": 7.919856374999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01MMVD8KtA8dUh3vwbE5u93N", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
